From b1917f8142d5cb066b63ec340988e114c710bb6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:22:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix stale 1m data (bug #1) and DST-safe Render cron gate (bug
 #2)

Bug #1: load_all_timeframes(cache_path=None) - the production path - never
ran the Live replay, so df_1m ended at now - DATA_LAG (3h) and signals.py
traded on a 3-hour-old "live" price with TEST_MODE=False.

- Historical pulls end at the dataset's published edge for ohlcv-1m
  (metadata.get_dataset_range), floored to the minute; DATA_LAG is now
  only the fallback if that lookup fails.
- Live intraday replay always runs, from (edge - 5 min) to the last closed
  minute; Historical wins on overlap.
- Fail closed: gateway ErrorMsg, early disconnect, timeout, callback
  exception, or a replay start outside the 24h window raise DataFeedError
  (ReplayTimeout also subclasses TimeoutError). run_signal_check already
  aborts the run on a data-load exception, so no orders go out.
- Collector no longer waits out the full timeout on gateway errors; the
  session is always stopped and closed.
- live_fill=False keeps a Historical-only path for research.

Bug #2: Render evaluates cron in UTC with no DST support. New schedule
*/4 12-20 * * 1-5 covers 08:00-16:00 ET under both offsets; run_signal_check
checks the ET wall clock (RUN_WINDOW_START/END, RUN_DAYS) and exits before
any data pull when outside it. Replaces unused RUN_HOURS.

Tests: 54 (fake network layer, real DBN record classes). The production
call site test fails on the old code with a last bar 3h stale.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GbXpWux8DHVYmDU2uwzwVi
